  "aiContextParagraph": "The Karthigai Deepam festival is the center of a developing legal and political dispute in Tamil Nadu, India. The controversy concerns the protocols for lighting the ceremonial lamp at the Tirupparankundram hill. Following initial government directives, a legal petition was filed with the Supreme Court of India to review the restrictions and procedures surrounding the event. The state government's approach to the matter has drawn public criticism from opposition figures, specifically the Bharatiya Janata Party, which has labeled the government's position as contrary to Hindu traditions. The Supreme Court is currently tasked with evaluating the petition, which aims to address the competing interests of religious practice and state administration. This situation remains an active point of debate, reflecting broader tensions regarding the oversight of religious rituals in the region and the intersection of judicial intervention and local governance.",
